---
title: "compute_requests_hash (Osaka Requests (EIP-7685): Contract-Triggered Request Processing)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_init: m = sha256()
    q_init --> q_iter: for request in requests
    q_iter --> q_hash: has next request
    q_hash --> q_update: digest = sha256(request).digest()
    q_update --> q_iter: m.update(digest)
    q_iter --> q_return: no more requests
    q_return --> [*]: return m.digest()
    note right of q_return
        INV-011: Each request is individually SHA-256 hashed before being fed into the outer hash
        INV-012: The hash is computed over requests in list order (order-dependent)
        INV-013: An empty requests list produces sha256() of empty input (the SHA-256 of nothing updated)
    end note
